 "task_id": "mng3-optimizer-shootout",
 "rung": 1,
 "title": "Five optimizers on the GPT-2-small speedrun setup, five runs each",
 "brief": {
  "text": "We're picking the optimizer for our small-GPT pretraining runs. optimizers/ has five training scripts, one per optimizer: baseline-muon, adamh, muonh, normuonh and psgd. They share the model (12 layers, 768 wide), the data (FineWeb, already tokenised under data/fineweb10B/) and the batch size; each sets its own step count. Each script runs on 1, 2 or 4 GPUs with torchrun and keeps the same global batch at any GPU count. Run every optimizer five times; the scripts are not seeded, so each run is a fresh sample. For each optimizer report the mean final validation loss and whether it clears 3.28 reliably: (3.28 - mean) x sqrt(n) >= 0.004. The machine has four H100s.",
  "provenance": "written by gpu-tasks from modded-nanogpt's records/track_3_optimization/README.md rules; it names no benchmark"
 },
